  "releaseNotes": "Kazo OS 3.5.2, changes for app developers:\n- The automatic services of a feature start at the login. In Kazo OS 3.5.1, an automatic service started at the login only if its code was already loaded, so the service of a feature stayed inactive (dead) until another entry point of the feature was launched. The OS now starts every enabled automatic service at the login and loads only the code of the services that start. An entry point of a feature may also start, stop and set the start mode of a service of its own feature (ADR 0286).\n- Test an app on the published trimmed OS. build/app-e2e/ holds a shared harness and a short test (smoke.mjs) that serve the published trimmed OS, install the app with kazopkg as the Store does, launch it and fail on a missing member, a kazopkg refusal or the app's failure panel. App repositories reach it through their Kazo OS submodule (ADR 0281).\nRelease notes: https://github.com/Kazo-ca/Os/releases/tag/v3.5.2",
